  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Paper Valley at Dawn",
    "overview": "ZonePlanner is a working instrument dressed in warm, layered paper. A cut-paper sunrise valley in peach, clay and sage crowns the page; the sage band closes in a waved paper contour, and the instrument's first cream card rests on that contour. Everything below the masthead is calm and legible: one meeting answer, a row of day strips, one gold bar dragged across all of them. The world comes from the user's inspiration image and keeps its materials (paper grain, soft sage-tinted lift, pill controls, a serif voice for answers) while dropping its decoration (rays, birds, trees, waterfalls).\n\nDensity is mobile-first and moderate: a single 720px column, 44px touch targets, 14px between stacked cards. The serif is reserved for what the page is saying (the wordmark, the meeting time, section titles); the grotesk carries every control and every number a person scans. Colour carries meaning first and mood second: sage is business and action, peach is the edge of the day, pale clay is the hours to avoid, gold is the thing you are holding, terracotta is the cost someone pays.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm paper neutrals only; no cool greys and no pure white surfaces.",
      "A layered-paper landscape masthead, sun without rays, five clay-to-sage ridges closed by a waved paper contour, each layer casting a soft upward paper shadow.",
      "Pills for every control; generous radii (22px cards, 26px sheet).",
      "Hour bands encoded twice: fill plus pattern or outline, never colour alone.",
      "One gold selection bar spanning every zone row; gold doubles as the focus ring.",
      "Tabular lining numerals everywhere a time appears."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two-Channel Band Rule",
        "body": "Every hour band carries a second channel besides hue: business is solid, edge is hatched at 135°, inconvenient is pale and outlined (hollow in marks). A band that only differs by colour is a bug.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Gold Is the Hand Rule",
        "body": "Gold marks only what the user is holding or focusing: the selection bar and focus rings. It never decorates, labels or warns.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Terracotta Is a Cost Rule",
        "body": "Terracotta appears only when someone pays for the chosen hour. It is never an accent, a button or a brand colour.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Serif Speaks the Answer Rule",
        "body": "Libre Baskerville is used only at 400 weight and only for the wordmark, the meeting time and section titles. Controls, zone names, data and labels are always Hanken Grotesk.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Time Rule",
        "body": "Every time, offset and hour tick uses tabular figures (`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`) so columns of times align and the headline does not jitter while dragging.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Answer-Above-the-Strips Rule",
        "body": "The meeting card (time, verdict, length, suggestions) always comes before the zone rows; the rows explain the answer, they never precede it.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat-on-the-Band Rule",
        "body": "Controls sitting on the sage masthead band drop Paper Lift; the band itself is their ground.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do encode every hour band twice: solid Business Sage, 135° hatched Dawn Peach, plain outlined Pale Clay, with a legend on the board.",
      "Do keep every touch target at least 44px and every control a pill.",
      "Do set the meeting time and section titles in Libre Baskerville 400, and everything a user taps or scans in Hanken Grotesk with tabular figures.",
      "Do lift cards with Paper Lift only; let controls on the sage band sit flat.",
      "Do reserve Lantern Gold for the selection bar and focus rings, and Terracotta for a cost someone pays.",
      "Do keep neutrals warm: draw new greys from the paper and clay family."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't distinguish bands by colour alone.",
      "Don't add rays, birds, trees or waterfalls to the masthead; the sun is a plain disc above layered ridges.",
      "Don't use gold or terracotta as decoration, branding or a button fill.",
      "Don't set controls, zone names or data in the serif, or the serif above 400 weight.",
      "Don't introduce cool greys, pure white surfaces or a second shadow style for cards."
    ]
  }
